attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a spine.** Columns 0 to 4, `mraZ` to `ilvI`, are carried by 95 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99 to 99.6% of them, fewest at column 4, `ilvI`, 99% {S1}.

@variable **A fork at column 5, `protein YabR`, carried by 64%**, opens the middle {S2, S2.c5}. Then the `leu` genes, columns 6 to 11, [[isopropylmalate dehydratase]] {S3, Q}. A branch at column 63, `IS4-like element IS421 family transposase`, runs in 44%, [[fimbria/pilus periplasmic chaperone]] {S10, S10.c63}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 93%, and hesitates less there, 0.21 against 0.26 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 59, `IS1 family transposase`, is a variable column, at 0.81 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on a fork and variable stretch.** Columns 73 to 79, `yaaX` to `yjjY`, are carried by 37 to 86% of chromosomes, all persistent {S12}. The last column is `yjjY`, in 37% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 96% of genes**, 0.22 bits on average, perplexity 1.2 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.81 against 0.20 bits, and names fewer genes, 74% against 96% {C}.

